reviewer: claude-opus-5-5 (self-review)
audience: Reviewers and implementers
purpose: How should engineering-system v0.1 be distributed, activated, locked per project and enforced?

Foundation v0.1 design: a single engsys plugin activated once per developer machine, a per-project contract of project.yaml plus lock.yaml, policy kept in YAML/schema/check code, and native tests/Git hooks/CI as the hard gate with Claude hooks as assistance only.
Translated from Korean to English without changing decisions, numbers (12-line route, 240-character description, 150-line skill body) or status; frontmatter left byte-identical.
Tables (draft decisions, component boundaries, guardrail matrix), the execution-flow text block and the next-design list keep their original rows and order; prose labels inside the text block were translated, commands and paths unchanged.
No Korean literals retained: the document has no Korean contract values.
The document has no summary paragraph before its first heading in the original, so none was added.
Deferred in .engsys/project.yaml; docs check reports 0 findings and link check passes. Self-review by the translating agent.

